[15.686419, "o", "<html><head><meta name=\"Keywords\" content=\"\" /><title>Founder Mode</title><!-- <META NAME=\"ROBOTS\" CONTENT=\"NOODP\"> -->\r\n<link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"http://ycombinator.com/arc/arc.png\">\r\n</head><body bgcolor=\"#ffffff\" background=\"https://s.turbifycdn.com/aah/paulgraham/bel-6.gif\" text=\"#000000\" link=\"#000099\" vlink=\"#464646\"><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr valign=\"top\"><td><map name=c39a69594cd7df><area shape=rect coords=\"0,0,67,21\" href=\"index.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,21,67,42\" href=\"articles.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,42,67,63\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/0596006624\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,63,67,84\" href=\"books.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,84,67,105\" href=\"http://ycombinator.com\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,105,67,126\" href=\"arc.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,126,67,147\" href=\"bel.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,147,67,168\" href=\"lisp.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,168,67,189\" href=\"antispam.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,189,67,210\" href=\"kedrosky.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,210,67,231\" href=\"faq.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,231,67,252\" href=\"raq.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,252,67,273\" href=\"quo.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,273,67,294\" href=\"rss.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,294,67,315\" href=\"bio.html\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,315,67,336\" href=\"https://twitter.com/paulg\"><area shape=rect coords=\"0,336,67,357\" href=\"https://mas.to/@paulg\"></map><img src=\"https://s.turbifycdn.com/aah/paulgraham/bel-7.gif\" width=\"69\" height=\"357\" usemap=#c39a69594cd7df border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" ismap /></td><td><img src=\"https://sep.turbifycdn.com/ca/Img/trans_1x1.gif\" height=\"1\" width=\"26\" border=\"0\" /></td><td><a href=\"index.html\"><img src=\"https://s.turbifycdn.com/aah/paulgraham/bel-8.gif\" width=\"410\" height=\"45\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" /></a><br /><br /><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"435\"><tr valign=\"top\"><td width=\"435\"><img src=\"https://s.turbifycdn.com/aah/paulgraham/founder-mode-1.gif\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" alt=\"Founder Mode\" /><br /><br /><font size=\"2\" face=\"verdana\">September 2024<br /><br />At a YC event last week Brian Chesky gave a talk that everyone who\r\nwas there will remember. Most founders I talked to afterward said\r\nit was the best they'd ever heard. Ron Conway, for the first time\r\nin his life, forgot to take notes. I'm not going to try to reproduce\r\nit here. Instead I want to talk about a question it raised.<br /><br />The theme of Brian's talk was that the conventional wisdom about\r\nhow to run larger companies is mistaken. As Airbnb grew, well-meaning\r\npeople advised him that he had to run the company in a certain way\r\nfor it to scale. Their advice could be optimistically summarized\r\nas \"hire good people and give them room to do their jobs.\" He\r\nfollowed this advice and the results were disastrous. So he had to\r\nfigure out a better way on his own, which he did partly by studying\r\nhow Steve Jobs ran Apple. So far it seems to be working. Airbnb's\r\nfree cash flow margin is now among the best in Silicon Valley.<br /><br />The audience at this event included a lot of the most successful\r\nfounders we've funded, and one after another said that the same\r\nthing had happened to them. They'd been given the same advice about\r\nhow to run their companies as they grew, but instead of helping\r\ntheir companies, it had damaged them.<br /><br />Why was everyone telling these founders the wrong thing? That was\r\nthe big mystery to me. And after mulling it over for a bit I figured\r\n"]
[15.693532, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@148e37eeecf8:~# "]
[27.587313, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > convert_essays.py\nimport requests\nimport os\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\ndef get_essay_text(url):\n    headers = {'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'}\n    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers)\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, 'html.parser')\n    # Paul Graham's essays are usually in a <font size=\"2\" face=\"verdana\"> tag\n    font_tag = soup.find('font', {'size': '2', 'face': 'verdana'})\n    if font_tag:\n        # Remove script and style elements\n        for script_or_style in font_tag([\"script\", \"style\"]):\n            script_or_style.decompose()\n        return font_tag.get_text(separator=' ', strip=True)\n    return soup.get_text(separator=' ', strip=True)\n\nessays = [\n    \"http://www.paulgraham.com/ds.html\",\n    \"http://www.paulgraham.com/foundermode.html\"\n]\n\ncombined_text = \"\"\nfor url in essays:\n    print(f\"Fetching {url}...\")\n    text = get_essay_text(url)\n    combined_text += text + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n# OpenAI TTS API has a limit of 4096 characters per request.\n# If the text is longer, we might need to split it.\n# Let's check the length.\nprint(f\"Total length: {len(combined_text)} characters\")\n\napi_key = os.getenv(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\nif not api_key:\n    print(\"Error: OPENAI_API_KEY not found.\")\n    exit(1)\n\n# Splitting text into chunks of 4000 characters to be safe\nchunks = [combined_text[i:i+4000] for i in range(0, len(combined_text), 4000)]\n\naudio_parts = []\nfor i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\n    print(f\"Converting chunk {i+1}/{len(chunks)} to speech...\")\n    response = requests.post(\n        \"https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/speech\",\n        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"},\n        json={\n            \"model\": \"tts-1\",\n            \"input\": chunk,\n            \"voice\": \"alloy\"\n        }\n    )\n    if response.status_code == 200:\n        audio_parts.append(response.content)\n    else:\n        print(f\"Error from OpenAI API: {response.status_code} - {response.text}\")\n        exit(1)\n\nwith open(\"/root/audiobook.mp3\", \"wb\") as f:\n    for part in audio_parts:\n        f.write(part)\n\nprint(\"Audiobook saved to /root/audiobook.mp3\")\nEOF\n"]
